    "title": {
     "en": "Leaves to touch"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Gopu loves to touch and smell leaves. Some are rough and some are smooth. Raj's jamun tree has thick shiny leaves."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "roots",
     "stem",
     "leaf",
     "soil"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Plants have parts: roots, stem, leaves, flowers and fruits.\nRoots grow under the soil. They hold the plant firmly and take in water from the soil.\nThe stem holds up the plant and carries water to the leaves. Trees have a thick woody trunk.\nLeaves can be rough or smooth, small or big, thin or thick. Touch and smell different leaves to explore.\nLeaves make food for the plant using sunlight (additional, not in the textbook).\nThe jamun tree has thick shiny leaves, tiny white flowers and green fruits that turn red and then purple."
    }
